/*
:name: spec_syntax_enum_typed_no_eq
:type: error
:error: expected '=' after the enum name
*/
// qa.md Appendix §4: "Enums require `=`: `enum E = (a, b)`, `enum E:U8 = (a, b)`.
// `enum E:U8 (a, b)` (no `=`) is an error." (Q18 "Reject (use `=`)";
// docs 03-bundle.md: `enum V6:U8 (a, b)   // error: missing '='`).
// The diagnostic must point at the enum declaration itself.
enum V6:U8 (a, b)   // locate_error_here
cassert(V6.a != V6.b)
